(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #109. A second `Free` after a deep free must behave
 exactly like a second `Free` on a plain list (test 613): the outer block
 is already the shared `_released_list_header`, so the identity check
 refuses it before touching anything - the nested list/map it used to hold
 are not revisited or double-freed either, since the walk never runs a
 second time on the released header (its own length is 0).)

a list called inner is [1, 2, 3].
a list called outer is [inner, "x"].
Free outer.
Free outer.
On error print "already freed".
print outer's length.
print outer.
